                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                           <td>The elevated PSA level is unexpected in a 71-year-old female, as PSA is typically used to assess prostate health in males. This result may indicate a laboratory or sample identification error, or rarely, ectopic PSA production. Clinical correlation and repeat testing are recommended to clarify the finding.</td>
